+### Proposed: one skill writes guards
+
+**Status**: Proposed 2026-10-07 by an entropy-assessment agent run. Awaiting Justin's decision; not in force.
+**Context**: Two exported skills write guards to different contracts. `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 writes a docs + workflow delta guard wherever the repo's guard lives. `session-coherence-skill-generator` writes a session-coherence guard at `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md`, with modes, mechanical checks and operational-state checks. `entropy-assessment` routes only to the first, `INTENT.md` names only the assessment skills as the guard generator, and no entry records why the second was added (the bootstrap entry below calls it "the previous `session-coherence-skill-generator`").
+**Proposal**: `session-coherence-skill-generator` becomes the only skill that writes guards. `docs-first-planning-assessment` supplies its docs-first checks to it instead of writing a guard, in line with "Consolidate domain generators into single skill" (one process, not parallel scaffolding).
+**Alternatives**: Two writers split by repo shape (docs-first repos by `docs-first-planning-assessment`, others and young repos by the generator); or reduce the generator to its bootstrap mode.
+
+---
+
+### Proposed: what the validation batch measures, and where results go
+
+**Status**: Proposed 2026-10-07 by an entropy-assessment agent run. Awaiting Justin's decision; not in force.
+**Context**: "Farm broader entropic-immunity exploration" below sets the next loop as a larger set of open-source projects, tracking whether it "produces more merged PRs". `INTENT.md` "Scope boundary and next validation loop" (2026-04-07) sets docs-first planning repos and tracks clearer session recovery, fewer reintroduced stale ideas, more coherent docs and sharper feedback. No entry records the change of measure. Justin's recorded evidence of value is suggested changes being merged quickly (`explorations/2026-03-19-autopoiesis.md`, opening message; `explorations/2026-03-24-entropy-immune-system-conversation.md`, the reply proposing a new project). No location is named for per-run results.
+**Proposal**: Run the batch on docs-first planning repos, as "Specialize first" sets. Record both measures for each run: whether suggested changes were merged, and `INTENT.md`'s session measures. Record one line per run under the `TODO.md` Next Up item while the batch runs, and move patterns to `LEARNINGS.md`.
+**Alternative**: Keep only one of the two measures.
